    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nWhere location is paramount, seldom does an opportunity arise to purchase such a particularly unique property offering exceptional versatility and the flexibility to adapt to a variety of lifestyle requirements, including an expansive single residence, home and income potential, multi-generational living, home and work or a combination of all these. (sub to any nescessary PP)\n\nDating from 1967, the property was originally designed as a detached four-bedroom residence. Due to the topography of the site it was possible to incorporate three additional apartments beneath the main house, together with a two level swimming pool, creating a highly adaptable and substantial property of considerable mid-20th Century character, offering an abundance of potential to remodel or refurbish.\n\nIn an article published in Creation International Magazine in April 1968 the property is headlined as Tomorrow's House Today!\n\nThe design was so innovative for its time, all straight lines, except where skirting the curves of the swimming pool in two areas , with no alcoves or wasted spaces. Large picture windows and glazed doors infuse the accommodation with natural light. The main house comprising 171.6 sqm approx is approached by a paved forecourt leading to the entrance hall. Inside there are two wings either side, one incorporating the living accommodation, the other houses the 4 bedrooms. The centre and dividing section is the kitchen dining room right in the heart of the home leading out to the sun deck and swimming pool.\n\nTwo of the apartments, no's 10 A and 10 B beneath the main house face south onto La Touche Park. 10A comprising c. 49.3 sqm contains a bed sitting room with entrance way, kitchen, shower room and two storage rooms. 10 B extending to c.86.9 sqm consists of an entrance porch, living room, kitchen, 2 bedrooms and shower room. 10 C is accessed from the east side garden and comprises a large open plan sunroom, living room and kitchen, bedroom and bathroom extending to. c.93.9 sqm.\n\nThe site extends to approximately a quarter acre and has the benefit of two vehicular gated entranceways, one having an electric gate, and a pedestrian gate. There is a lovely lawned garden interspersed with fruit trees to the east side together with strategically placed patio and deck areas for all day sunshine. There is also a covered carport ideal for many storage uses in the north west corner.\n\nThe location itself needs little introduction with the wealth of amenities on its doorstep. A short walk into the heart of Greystones which boasts an enviable array of coffee shops, cafes, restaurants and boutiques. It is also around the corner from the harbour and marina board walk linking to the seafront and the Cove beach. The town has a vast choice of sporting and leisure facilities including the local Rugby, GAA, Soccer, Tennis, Sailing and bowling clubs, three beaches, Shoreline indoor swimming pool and fitness centre with the library and churches of several denominations all to hand. The many local primary and secondary schools, many within walking distance have excellent reputations. There are a variety of exceptional golf courses in the locality Greystones, Delgany, Druids Heath, Powerscourt and Bray to name but a few. Transport links include the DART and mainline station, TFI local L 1, 2 & 3 and X1 & 2 bus routes serving the locality, Blackrock and Dublin City and easy access to the N11/M50 network."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nNo. 10 - \n\n\nEntrance Hall: - \nShower Room & Cloakroom\n\nLiving Room: - 5.67m x 9.55m\nTriple aspect room, fire place, Doors & outside terrace leading to swimming pool, Door to:\n\nKitchen / Dining Room: - 4.05m x 8.32m\nSolid oak cabinetry with granite work tops, Neff double oven & microwave, Integrated F.F., double bowl SS sink, Neff electric hob with overhead extractor, Solid fuel stove, Parquet flooring. Centre island, Door out to pool.\n\nBedroom 1: - 4.04m x 3.43m\nSink. Wardrobe & vanity unit.\n\nEn Suite: - 1.91m x 3.00m\nBath, WC & WHB.\n\nBedroom 2: - 4.04m x 3.88m\nWHB & wardrobe small single, Hot Press.\n\nBathroom: - 2.99m x 1.95m\n3-piece suite & bath, Extensively tiled.\n\nBedroom 3: - 2.99m x 2.27\nSink, WHB & under storage, Built in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 4: - 4.90m x 1.90m\nDouble WHB & wardrobes overlooking pool.\n\nNo. 10A - \n\n\nPlant Room & Pool Boiler - \n\n\nEntrance Hall: - \nLeading to Living Room, Parquet floor,\n\nLiving/Bedroom: - 4.82m x 4.01m\nwall shelving, Sliding screen to:\n\nKitchen: - \nStainless Steel sink unit, fitted floor & wall presses.\n\nBack hall: - \nLeading to:\n\nShower Room: - \n3-piece suite with storage closet off with immersion heater.\n\nNo. 10B - \n\n\nEntrance lobby: - \nLeading to, Living/Kitchen & Bedroom 2\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining Room: - 6.62m x 7.96m\nFitted floor & wall cabinets, Breakfast counter, Slot-in Tricity cooker, Timber T&G ceiling.\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.92m x 5.80m\nDouble large bedroom, Fitted wardrobes, large window, serviced by:\n\nEn Suite: - 3.92m x 2.16m\nShower room, large step-in shower, WHB & WC, Hot press.\n\nBedroom 2: - 3.24m x 5.94m\nFitted wardrobes, Serviced by:\n\nEn Suite: - \nWHB & WC (No shower).\n\nNo. 10C - \n\n\nSunroom: - 4.89m x 6.88m\nLeading to:\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining - 6.20m x 8.01m\nLarge self-contained unit currently uesd as an art studio, large open plan Kitchen/Living/Dining room, Solid wood floor & wall cabinets, Stainless steel sink unit, Electric & gas hobs. Plaster ceiling roof. Door to loft & window to front garden, Solid fuel stove, door leading to:\n\nBedroom - 3.98m x 4.12m\nLarge Double bedroom, window to open plan space, Timber boarded floor, serviced by:\n\nBathroom: - 2.22m x 4.12m\n3-piece en-suite, parquet floor, Hot press.\n\n"
